  "body": "## Summary\n\nThis adds an independent, data-only closure audit of the frozen replay capsule behind the selected PR1042 result. It changes no construction, selected certificate, or \u03ba.\n\n- **Track:** Independent verification/formalization\n- **OS-random seed:** 75\n- **Exact base:** `ba82555c64e1879e4b7decce28186f208fcb8262`\n- **Selected \u03ba:** `1672188119205421 / 10^18`\n- **Audited capsule:** `research/community-frontier1042-audit/selected-replay.tar.gz`\n\n## Result\n\nThe standard-library verifier treats the archive as untrusted data, never extracts members, and imports no construction code. It verifies:\n\n- 458 unique, relative, regular, non-executable members.\n- 45,647,427 expanded bytes.\n- Exact SHA-256 agreement for all 457 declared artifacts.\n- Exact inventory closure: no missing or undeclared artifact.\n- The fixed ten-stage sequence, zero exit codes, and all stage-log bindings.\n- Byte equality for six promoted repository receipts.\n- Agreement among the capsule, selected record, and batch integration receipt for the selected value, audited source head, certificate, source manifest, and archive pins.\n\nNo discrepancy was found. This is independent publication-evidence verification, not a new \u03ba claim.\n\n## Reproduce\n\n```sh\nmake frontier1042-capsule-closure-verify\n```\n\nExpected final output:\n\n```text\nPASS_FRONTIER1042_CAPSULE_CLOSURE\nRan 6 tests\nOK\n```\n\nThe target also runs the verifier under optimized Python and compares both generated receipts byte-for-byte with the committed `RESULT.json`.\n\n## Negative controls\n\nThe focused test suite requires rejection of:\n\n1. Path traversal.\n2. Duplicate archive members.\n3. An undeclared member.\n4. Mutated artifact bytes.\n5. A nonzero replay-stage exit code.\n6. A promoted-receipt mismatch.\n\n## Overlap\n\nThis does not repeat the invoice and outer-arithmetic recomputation in PR #1112 or the existing T16 owner-map audits. It checks the distinct question of whether the frozen selected replay archive forms a complete, path-safe, byte-authenticated evidence capsule.\n\n## Scope\n\nThis finite audit authenticates archive bytes and publication bindings relative to exact pins. It does not establish that the recorded commands ran, independently recompute the construction mathematics, verify every named source package, discharge inherited all-size/compiler or realization interfaces, prove analytic transfer, or formalize the multiplication theorem.\n\nThe selected frontier and `upstream/` are unchanged.\n\n## Attribution\n\nContribution by Martin Rv (@martinxxx9), with substantial Perplexity AI assistance in research, implementation, verification, and writing. PR1042, batch1047, and predecessor construction/review attribution remain with their original contributors.\n\nNew material is Apache-2.0.\n",
